{"nodes": [{"id": "brain_log_62_r6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result_r6_wlsv_unbiasedness", "label": "R6 \u2014 the unbiasedness precondition WLS_v inherits from MinT", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "brain/log/62_R6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_log_62_r6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result_wickramasuriya_optimal_2019", "label": "wickramasuriya_optimal_2019 \u2014 MinT optimality", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "brain/log/62_R6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_log_62_r6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result_unbiasedness_check", "label": "unbiasedness_check() in hierarchy/reconcile.py", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/log/62_R6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One-sample t-test of mean(residual)=0 per node on the held-out calibration block; no multiplicity correction because the quantity of interest is the direction and size of bias, not a family-wise decision."}, {"id": "brain_log_62_r6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result_unbiasedness_precondition", "label": "Unbiased-base precondition for MinT/WLS_v", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/log/62_R6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The 2019 paper does not address biased bases at all; the honest form of the project's claim is therefore conditional, and until this run the condition was assumed."}, {"id": "brain_log_62_r6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result_dow_median_base_bias", "label": "The day-of-week median base is biased on 22 of 41 nodes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/log/62_R6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A median is median-eliciting, so on a right-skewed node it sits below the mean; 19 of the 22 violations are positive, which is that prediction cashed out rather than a bug."}, {"id": "brain_log_62_r6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result_hewamalage_forecast_2023", "label": "hewamalage_forecast_2023 \u2014 absolute-error measures optimise the median", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "brain/log/62_R6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_log_62_r6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result_kolassa_we_2023", "label": "kolassa_we_2023 \u2014 coherence and elicitation", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "brain/log/62_R6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_log_62_r6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result_measurement_argument_chain", "label": "The four-link measurement argument chain", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/log/62_R6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Absolute-error measures elicit the median; median-eliciting forecasts are usually not coherent; MinT optimality needs unbiased bases; our DOW-median bases are measurably biased. One of the few places the project's own data supplies empirical support for a theoretical objection its literature review makes."}, {"id": "brain_log_62_r6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result_d_f7", "label": "D-F7 \u2014 conformance row R22", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/log/62_R6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "brain_log_62_r6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result_r6_wlsv_unbiasedness", "target": "brain_log_62_r6_wlsv_unbiasedness_result_unbiasedness